msgstr "Same trusted serialized management as close/join; never an untrusted wire action. The kernel decides when cleanup is authorized. First close/cancel and separately drive the real owner. Every retained exact cell must acquire SETTLED and the owner must be idle. The trusted drained proof then fences future gateway entries and joins all outer observers while retaining the role. Only then are all copied payloads wiped and cells retired without user copyout. Pending, quarantined or unjoined work retains every cell unchanged. Success is idempotent and permanently rejects dispatch. It does not release the role: successful join is still required before reclaiming any bound storage. No forced borrow revocation, process-liveness policy or provider service is supplied."

