msgstr "SUBMIT proposes the exact next nonzero 64-bit epoch for an explicit slot within the exact claimed nonzero session and supplies positive length plus an absolute deadline in the existing owner's clock domain. Other actions use the accepted exact epoch and zero length/deadline words. device must match the immutable trusted binding; reserved=0. Word pairs encode low then high halves, independently of the compiler enum, pointer and uint64_t alignment ABI. These are local C gateway records; an integrating kernel owns byte order and any transport serialization."

