msgstr "[inout] Exact caller-owned cells/payloads, no maximum pool."

msgid "[in] Positive cell count representable in a scalar slot ID."
msgstr "[in] Positive cell count representable in a scalar slot ID."

msgid "[in] Immutable trusted principal/grant/copy/owner binding."
msgstr "[in] Immutable trusted principal/grant/copy/owner binding."

msgid "SUCCESS or INVALID/STATE/CONTEXT/BUSY/EXHAUSTED, or trusted claim error without new retained users or hardware effects; every rejected output remains unchanged."
msgstr "SUCCESS or INVALID/STATE/CONTEXT/BUSY/EXHAUSTED, or trusted claim error without new retained users or hardware effects; every rejected output remains unchanged."

msgid "Nominal actual user RAM; trusted copy still enforces real access."
msgstr "Nominal actual user RAM; trusted copy still enforces real access."

msgid "Bounded trusted kernel identity and fault-contained copies."
msgstr "Bounded trusted kernel identity and fault-contained copies."

msgid "identity authenticates the current entry, never user input. Copy operations guarantee complete checked CPU access and mapping/process lifetime for the callback duration. Neither success nor error retains a user address, kernel scratch pointer, mapping or observer after return. Errors may have partially copied bytes; the copied payload cell is wiped on rejection, and reply failure is recoverable through exact slot/epoch. No callback blocks, dispatches recursively, or substitutes a permission observation for fault-safe copying. Identity/copy callbacks may close this mediation. A new kernel/CMSE wrapper must actually establish these preconditions; this component does not.              claim is a trusted exclusive role authority for the actual              owner/controller binding. It rejects a second live role even              with a larger session, and rejects reused/non-increasing              nonzero sessions from persistent, nonwrapping history across              fresh storage, process/device reset and reconstruction.              Failed claim retains no reference/effect. Successful claim              permanently consumes that session and retains the exact role              until release. release SUCCESS proves outer gateway/transport observers joined and detaches all authority references; failure retains the original role unchanged. drained SUCCESS permanently fences future outer gateway entry and joins all gateway/transport observers, while the exact role remains claimed. Failed drained preserves the role and every cell unchanged. It must not modify bound configuration, cell identities or requests. Claim, release and drained are bounded and cannot recursively construct, dispatch, close, reap or join. Context/history must remain live; no source code implements this kernel authority, physical isolation, storage partition or recovery policy. Alternate wrappers of one controller are not distinct roles."
msgstr "identity authenticates the current entry, never user input. Copy operations guarantee complete checked CPU access and mapping/process lifetime for the callback duration. Neither success nor error retains a user address, kernel scratch pointer, mapping or observer after return. Errors may have partially copied bytes; the copied payload cell is wiped on rejection, and reply failure is recoverable through exact slot/epoch. No callback blocks, dispatches recursively, or substitutes a permission observation for fault-safe copying. Identity/copy callbacks may close this mediation. A new kernel/CMSE wrapper must actually establish these preconditions; this component does not.              claim is a trusted exclusive role authority for the actual              owner/controller binding. It rejects a second live role even              with a larger session, and rejects reused/non-increasing              nonzero sessions from persistent, nonwrapping history across              fresh storage, process/device reset and reconstruction.              Failed claim retains no reference/effect. Successful claim              permanently consumes that session and retains the exact role              until release. release SUCCESS proves outer gateway/transport observers joined and detaches all authority references; failure retains the original role unchanged. drained SUCCESS permanently fences future outer gateway entry and joins all gateway/transport observers, while the exact role remains claimed. Failed drained preserves the role and every cell unchanged. It must not modify bound configuration, cell identities or requests. Claim, release and drained are bounded and cannot recursively construct, dispatch, close, reap or join. Context/history must remain live; no source code implements this kernel authority, physical isolation, storage partition or recovery policy. Alternate wrappers of one controller are not distinct roles."

msgid "Immutable trusted one-principal/one-device/one-owner grant."
msgstr "Immutable trusted one-principal/one-device/one-owner grant."

msgid "This is kernel configuration, never copied from users. owner/executor/port must be the already constructed exact BusOwner + UARTOwner bridge, with no other direct producers or external request/payload observers. Completion callbacks are not installed. All callback contexts remain privileged; explicit extents cover their complete live controls. Guard, clock and wake contexts may be the same trusted object. The caller owns actual UART startup, hardware attribution, executor scheduling, clock/deadline domain and final stop."
msgstr "This is kernel configuration, never copied from users. owner/executor/port must be the already constructed exact BusOwner + UARTOwner bridge, with no other direct producers or external request/payload observers. Completion callbacks are not installed. All callback contexts remain privileged; explicit extents cover their complete live controls. Guard, clock and wake contexts may be the same trusted object. The caller owns actual UART startup, hardware attribution, executor scheduling, clock/deadline domain and final stop."

msgid "Exact privileged cell; initialize only data and capacity."
msgstr "Exact privileged cell; initialize only data and capacity."

msgid "All other fields start zero and are mechanism-private after construction. data is independent writable privileged RAM, capacity is its exact positive byte budget, at most UINT32_MAX. No user pointer is ever assigned here. Core identity epochs never wrap and survive consume/close; never copy or reset a live cell. UARTOwner borrows operation/payload until real provider final access, then user-result retention lasts until successful reply copy plus joined CONSUME, or trusted joined reap. Epoch history survives both paths."
msgstr "All other fields start zero and are mechanism-private after construction. data is independent writable privileged RAM, capacity is its exact positive byte budget, at most UINT32_MAX. No user pointer is ever assigned here. Core identity epochs never wrap and survive consume/close; never copy or reset a live cell. UARTOwner borrows operation/payload until real provider final access, then user-result retention lasts until successful reply copy plus joined CONSUME, or trusted joined reap. Epoch history survives both paths."

msgid "Caller-owned trusted control; initialize once, never reset epochs."
msgstr "Caller-owned trusted control; initialize once, never reset epochs."

msgid "i3c_controller.h"
msgstr "i3c_controller.h"

msgid "Explicit bounded I3C discovery, transfers and event ownership."
msgstr "Explicit bounded I3C discovery, transfers and event ownership."

msgid "Prepare unused metadata without retaining its payload."
msgstr "Prepare unused metadata without retaining its payload."

msgid "Serialized owner Thread. DISCOVER has no payload or target. PRIVATE permits 1..65535 bytes. CCC permits only ENEC/DISEC broadcast/direct writes and direct GETMWL/GETMRL/GETPID/ GETBCR/GETDCR/GETSTATUS reads, with exact defined lengths. GETMRL uses two bytes, or three when confirmed BCR bit2 advertises an IBI payload. Address-changing, HDR and controller-handoff CCCs reject. All APIs require one serialized executor. Port and clock callbacks must not reenter the core, invoke application code or mutate retained state. No ISR, allocation, OS lock or worker. Absolute deadlines use the injected clock."
msgstr "Serialized owner Thread. DISCOVER has no payload or target. PRIVATE permits 1..65535 bytes. CCC permits only ENEC/DISEC broadcast/direct writes and direct GETMWL/GETMRL/GETPID/ GETBCR/GETDCR/GETSTATUS reads, with exact defined lengths. GETMRL uses two bytes, or three when confirmed BCR bit2 advertises an IBI payload. Address-changing, HDR and controller-handoff CCCs reject. All APIs require one serialized executor. Port and clock callbacks must not reenter the core, invoke application code or mutate retained state. No ISR, allocation, OS lock or worker. Absolute deadlines use the injected clock."

msgid "Admit a finite operation after cold validation and readiness."
msgstr "Admit a finite operation after cold validation and readiness."

msgid "SUCCESS transfers the borrow. Rejection has no effects or retained references. Outputs cannot alias retained controller, port table, target/event storage, policy, request or payload. Port and clock context spans remain the caller's responsibility."
msgstr "SUCCESS transfers the borrow. Rejection has no effects or retained references. Outputs cannot alias retained controller, port table, target/event storage, policy, request or payload. Port and clock context spans remain the caller's responsibility."

msgid "Perform one bounded FIFO/event phase or one drain proof."
msgstr "Perform one bounded FIFO/event phase or one drain proof."

msgid "Partial DAA, malformed observations and errors fault admission while retaining every known/tentative assigned address. Cancel/timeout/failed drain never release a loan. Failed quiescence stays QUARANTINED; continued service may recover. An event overflow returns OVERFLOW and latches its counter, without discarding an already retained queued event."
msgstr "Partial DAA, malformed observations and errors fault admission while retaining every known/tentative assigned address. Cancel/timeout/failed drain never release a loan. Failed quiescence stays QUARANTINED; continued service may recover. An event overflow returns OVERFLOW and latches its counter, without discarding an already retained queued event."

msgid "Request withdrawal using stable epoch before request dereference."
msgstr "Request withdrawal using stable epoch before request dereference."

msgid "Obtain only a confirmed target; tentative/retired records reject."
msgstr "Obtain only a confirmed target; tentative/retired records reject."

msgid "Copy one retained event; EMPTY leaves output unchanged."
msgstr "Copy one retained event; EMPTY leaves output unchanged."

msgid "Copy saturating loss counters without clearing them."
msgstr "Copy saturating loss counters without clearing them."

msgid "Close admission without changing loans, target identities or events."
msgstr "Close admission without changing loans, target identities or events."

msgid "Prove a whole-bus reset before invalidating dynamic addresses."
msgstr "Prove a whole-bus reset before invalidating dynamic addresses."

msgid "Requires closed admission. Hardware proof covers real wire, FIFO and IRQ quiescence AND every target's dynamic address invalidated. Peripheral reset or FIFO flush alone is never this proof. Failure preserves all loans and address records. Success settles outstanding work and invalidates endpoints; retained events preserve their old epochs for the caller."
msgstr "Requires closed admission. Hardware proof covers real wire, FIFO and IRQ quiescence AND every target's dynamic address invalidated. Peripheral reset or FIFO flush alone is never this proof. Failure preserves all loans and address records. Success settles outstanding work and invalidates endpoints; retained events preserve their old epochs for the caller."

msgid "Reopen an idle unfaulted pause; faults require explicit bus reset."
msgstr "Reopen an idle unfaulted pause; faults require explicit bus reset."

msgid "Close, withdraw and finally relinquish the unique controller."
msgstr "Close, withdraw and finally relinquish the unique controller."

msgid "Active work or queued events return BUSY. Caller continues service, consumes events and retries. Assigned/tentative addresses or a fault return STATE until whole-bus reset proof invalidates them. Successful final wire/ FIFO/IRQ quiescence releases ownership, never reconstructing this object. Storage outlives copied endpoints and tickets."
msgstr "Active work or queued events return BUSY. Caller continues service, consumes events and retries. Assigned/tentative addresses or a fault return STATE until whole-bus reset proof invalidates them. Successful final wire/ FIFO/IRQ quiescence releases ownership, never reconstructing this object. Storage outlives copied endpoints and tickets."

msgid "Controller-bound confirmed target incarnation, never a factory ID."
msgstr "Controller-bound confirmed target incarnation, never a factory ID."

msgid "Stable operation identity; controller outlives all copied controls."
msgstr "Stable operation identity; controller outlives all copied controls."

msgid "Caller-owned finite operation; no implicit bus discovery."
msgstr "Caller-owned finite operation; no implicit bus discovery."

msgid "Initialize base once with nx_request_initialize. Accepted metadata and payload stay borrowed until acquire SETTLED. TX stays immutable; transferred counts bytes handed to the FIFO, not acknowledged target effects. No replay after errors. Public fields are immutable throughout an accepted borrow."
msgstr "Initialize base once with nx_request_initialize. Accepted metadata and payload stay borrowed until acquire SETTLED. TX stays immutable; transferred counts bytes handed to the FIFO, not acknowledged target effects. No replay after errors. Public fields are immutable throughout an accepted borrow."

msgid "Copied event; no callback, target creation or hidden work."
msgstr "Copied event; no callback, target creation or hidden work."

msgid "IBI endpoint retains its exact confirmed target epoch. Confirmed BCR bit1 must advertise IBI. Bit2 requires 1..4 payload bytes including MDB; otherwise zero data bytes. HOT_JOIN carries no endpoint and only requests explicit caller-controlled discovery. Payload is at most four bytes, as in the selected H563 reference; no timestamp claim."
msgstr "IBI endpoint retains its exact confirmed target epoch. Confirmed BCR bit1 must advertise IBI. Bit2 requires 1..4 payload bytes including MDB; otherwise zero data bytes. HOT_JOIN carries no endpoint and only requests explicit caller-controlled discovery. Payload is at most four bytes, as in the selected H563 reference; no timestamp claim."

msgid "Explicit loss accounting; counters saturate rather than wrap."
msgstr "Explicit loss accounting; counters saturate rather than wrap."

msgid "i3c_controller_storage.h"
