msgstr "One bounded hardware observation and aggregate FIFO progress."

msgid "No callback retains spans. tx/rx counts may not exceed the supplied capacities. DAA acknowledged confirms the preceding assignment BEFORE any next identity in this observation. A complete DAA with a tentative unacknowledged address is an error, never implicit success. Event data are fully copied."
msgstr "No callback retains spans. tx/rx counts may not exceed the supplied capacities. DAA acknowledged confirms the preceding assignment BEFORE any next identity in this observation. A complete DAA with a tentative unacknowledged address is an error, never implicit success. Event data are fully copied."

msgid "Synchronous bounded hardware leaves; no request forwarding."
msgstr "Synchronous bounded hardware leaves; no request forwarding."

msgid "begin and assign are infallible commands. pump reports later hardware failures and services at most the supplied batch capacities plus one IBI and one hot-join latch. No command or span is retained. No application code is called. withdraw requests abort. quiescent SUCCESS proves actual wire/FIFO/IRQ quiescence and all port observers detached."
msgstr "begin and assign are infallible commands. pump reports later hardware failures and services at most the supplied batch capacities plus one IBI and one hot-join latch. No command or span is retained. No application code is called. withdraw requests abort. quiescent SUCCESS proves actual wire/FIFO/IRQ quiescence and all port observers detached."

msgid "reset additionally proves EVERY target dynamic address invalidated. FIFO flush or controller reset alone cannot report SUCCESS. BUSY/IO/UNSUPPORTED proof retains loans and ownership. release follows successful final quiescence. The port context and supplied storage outlive observers."
msgstr "reset additionally proves EVERY target dynamic address invalidated. FIFO flush or controller reset alone cannot report SUCCESS. BUSY/IO/UNSUPPORTED proof retains loans and ownership. release follows successful final quiescence. The port context and supplied storage outlive observers."

msgid "All port/clock callbacks are non-reentrant: no core calls, application calls or mutation of retained core state. claim atomically acquires an exclusive controller and its IRQ/clock/pins. SUCCESS requires independently established proof that EVERY target dynamic address is invalidated, including targets still powered across MCU reset. The caller establishes this baseline before construction; claim never attempts an unproven reset. Rejection has no effects. ready is a read-only admission check."
msgstr "All port/clock callbacks are non-reentrant: no core calls, application calls or mutation of retained core state. claim atomically acquires an exclusive controller and its IRQ/clock/pins. SUCCESS requires independently established proof that EVERY target dynamic address is invalidated, including targets still powered across MCU reset. The caller establishes this baseline before construction; claim never attempts an unproven reset. Rejection has no effects. ready is a read-only admission check."

msgid "Exact caller capacities; separate static controller and target data."
msgstr "Exact caller capacities; separate static controller and target data."

msgid "Open the fixed AlarmA-copy delegate for the same concrete Stop2 owner."
msgstr "Open the fixed AlarmA-copy delegate for the same concrete Stop2 owner."

msgid "All ordinary initialization preconditions remain required. Unlike the WUT-only initializer, this explicitly delegates fixed AlarmA compare registers, ALRAE and ALRAF/CALRAF to the same serialized wake owner. ALRAIE and automatic flag clearing stay forbidden. The fixed profile masks all calendar fields and compares no subseconds, producing its first event on a seconds increment. Both alarm registers start zero. The delegate preserves the calendar/source and owns complete producer withdrawal before any compound copy settlement. No AlarmA factory, arbitrary alarm scheduler or second RTC writer is admitted."
msgstr "All ordinary initialization preconditions remain required. Unlike the WUT-only initializer, this explicitly delegates fixed AlarmA compare registers, ALRAE and ALRAF/CALRAF to the same serialized wake owner. ALRAIE and automatic flag clearing stay forbidden. The fixed profile masks all calendar fields and compares no subseconds, producing its first event on a seconds increment. Both alarm registers start zero. The delegate preserves the calendar/source and owns complete producer withdrawal before any compound copy settlement. No AlarmA factory, arbitrary alarm scheduler or second RTC writer is admitted."

